INSERT INTO `clientRequests` VALUES (1,'haris','ellahi','2025-02-20','','',NULL,'sdhgsdh','jsdhjh','cdhjh','7887','565656565656','haris@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'sdsdh',55,1,0,0,0,'2025-02-14 07:49:21','2025-02-14 07:49:21',NULL,'scheduled',NULL),(2,'hhsdshd','hsaghd','2025-02-27','','',NULL,'usdjhshdhg','sghasg','jhadh','899','87888888888','haris@gmail.com','7888888888888',NULL,'djdg',77,0,1,0,0,'2025-02-17 05:17:33','2025-02-17 05:17:33','Porter','scheduled',NULL),(3,'ibrahim','khan','2025-01-30','','',NULL,'gfsdfsfd','sdfsfd','gsdfdgf','65454','rrrwetrwetr','text@rwest.com',NULL,NULL,'hsdghsdgh',6,0,1,0,0,'2025-02-17 07:32:59','2025-02-27 10:46:16','Haris Ellahi','completed','1. Mr. Ibrahim, can you elaborate on what your main objectives are with your Life Insurance? Are you primarily focused on estate planning, income replacement, or another goal?\n2. Based on your current Life Insurance coverage, do you feel it is adequate to cover your family\'s needs in the event of any unfortunate incident?\n3. Given your current lifestyle and family obligations, how much income would your family need per year if you were no longer there to provide for them?\n4. Have there been any significant changes in your life recently such as marriage, birth of a child, purchase of a new home, or retirement that may affect your life insurance needs?\n5. Are you familiar with the different types of Life Insurance policies available, such as term life, whole life, or universal life? Do you have a preference for any of these?\n6. Do you have any specific concerns or questions regarding your current Life Insurance policy that you would like us to address?\n7. Are you interested in exploring Life Insurance policies that could potentially offer a cash value component for wealth accumulation?\n8. Considering your present and future financial obligations, have you thought about the impact of potential health care costs or long-term care needs on your financial plan?\n9. Do you have any plans or provisions in place for estate conservation? How does your current Life Insurance plan fit into this?\n10. Are you interested in learning about ways to potentially maximize the benefits from your Life Insurance policy, beyond just the death benefit?'),(4,'haris','ellahi','2025-02-06','','',NULL,'hgvdshgshre','hdghsg','ggdhsg','5656','65656565656','haris@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'gshghgdhg',776,1,0,0,0,'2025-02-18 05:07:10','2025-02-25 04:36:53','Haris Ellahi','completed','1. What is your current understanding of Medicare, and do you have any specific aspects you would like to explore further?\n2. Are you currently enrolled in any Medicare plan, or is this your first time considering such coverage?\n3. If you are enrolled in a Medicare plan, are there any aspects of your coverage that you are not satisfied with or feel could be improved?\n4. Have you thought about your long-term health needs and how a Medicare plan may assist in addressing them?\n5. Are there any specific health concerns or medical conditions that you believe should be specifically addressed in your Medicare plan?\n6. Have you considered how Medicare fits into your overall wealth and long-term care planning strategy?\n7. Do you have any other forms of health or life insurance, and if so, how do you see Medicare complementing these existing plans?\n8. Are you aware of the potential out-of-pocket costs associated with Medicare, and have you planned for these in your financial planning?\n9. What are your primary goals when it comes to securing a Medicare plan, and what are your main concerns?\n10. What changes, if any, do you anticipate in your healthcare needs in the coming years, and how would you like your Medicare plan to accommodate these changes?'),(5,'ali','ali','2025-02-10','','',NULL,'hsfgsfd','gshdfgh','zsgxf','6565','6545454545454','haris@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'fsdsgf',56,0,0,0,1,'2025-02-18 05:26:23','2025-02-26 10:16:16','Haris Ellahi','completed','1. What are your primary objectives for long-term care planning? Are there specific needs or preferences you have in mind?\n2. Have you already taken any steps towards planning for your long-term care? If yes, could you please provide more details?\n3. How much have you budgeted or set aside for your long-term care needs?\n4. Do you have any existing health conditions that we should consider while planning for your long-term care?\n5. Have you considered the potential need for assistance with daily activities in the future such as bathing, dressing, or meal preparation?\n6. Do you have a preference for receiving care at home or in a residential care facility?\n7. Are there any family or friends who would be involved in your care? What is their capacity to assist and what are their thoughts on your long-term care planning?\n8. Have you considered the potential impact of long-term care costs on your current lifestyle and wealth?\n9. Do you have any existing insurance policies that could contribute towards your long-term care costs?\n10. What are your primary concerns about long-term care planning and what would you like to achieve through our meeting today?'),(6,'mousa ','ali','2025-01-30','','',NULL,'sahdgshgdh','vxsgfdh','sdgsfdg','56324562','234524352435','haris@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'gashdgshdg',5,1,0,0,0,'2025-02-20 11:03:46','2025-02-26 07:43:23','Haris Ellahi','completed','1. What are your primary healthcare needs and how do you hope Medicare will address these needs?\n2. Do you have any specific concerns about your current healthcare coverage that you hope to address through Medicare?\n3. Are you currently enrolled in any other form of insurance or healthcare plan? If yes, could you share the details of these plans?\n4. Have you made any recent changes to your insurance policies, and if so, what were these changes?\n5. If you are retiring or planning to retire soon, how do you envision Medicare fitting into your retirement plan?\n6. Do you have any existing health conditions that require regular medical attention, and how do you hope Medicare can assist with this?\n7. Have you researched or considered any specific Medicare plans? If so, which ones and why?\n8. Are you familiar with how Medicare works with other insurance, and do you have any questions or concerns about this?\n9. What is your understanding of the benefits of Medicare and are there any areas you would like more information on?\n10. What is your preferred method of communication for receiving Medicare information and updates? Would you be comfortable setting up a secure Medicare account for email notifications?'),(7,'HARRY','POTER','2025-02-06','','',NULL,'dha ','lahore','Punjab','5151','0101010100','haris@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'ali',2,0,0,1,0,'2025-02-27 11:05:27','2025-02-28 05:21:16','Haris Ellahi','completed','1. What are your primary financial goals that you hope to achieve with wealth planning?\n2. How stable is your income from your retirement account(s) and real estate, and how do they factor into your current financial planning?\n3. You mentioned a distribution plan, can you share more about it and its role in your wealth planning strategy?\n4. In terms of estate planning, can you provide more details about your will and living trust? How do they fit into your overall wealth management plan?\n5. Do you have any specific concerns about how estate laws might impact your current wealth and future inheritance?\n6. How important is it for you to maintain your current lifestyle post-retirement, and what steps have you taken towards this?\n7. You expressed worry about figuring out how much you need for retirement. Can you share more about this concern?\n8. You mentioned wanting to reduce your Social Security Taxation. Can you explain your current situation and why you feel this is necessary?\n9. How critical is it for you to maintain your spouse\'s lifestyle in your wealth planning?\n10. Are there any specific issues or concerns you have regarding your Irrevocable Grantor Trust that you would like to discuss?'),(8,'imran','khan','2025-01-30','','',NULL,'bani gala','islamabad','punjab','767676','99999999999','imrankhan@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'qasim',2,1,0,0,0,'2025-02-28 06:03:54','2025-02-28 06:06:43','Haris Ellahi','completed','1. Can you provide some insight into your current health status and any ongoing treatments or medical conditions you have? This will help us understand what Medicare plan might be most beneficial for you.\n2. What are your main goals when it comes to your Medicare plan? Are you looking for comprehensive coverage, or do you have specific areas you want to focus on?\n3. Do you have any particular concerns or apprehensions about Medicare that you\'d like us to address?\n4. Have you previously enrolled in any Medicare plan? If yes, could you share your experiences or issues if any?\n5. Could you please tell us about any other existing health insurance plans you have? This is important as we need to understand how Medicare will work with your other insurance.\n6. Are you considering retirement in the near future? If so, have you thought about how this might affect your health coverage needs?\n7. Do you have any dependents who are also in need of health coverage? If so, what are their health needs?\n8. How comfortable are you with out-of-pocket costs? Understanding your comfort level will help us suggest a plan that fits your financial situation.\n9. Are you looking for any specific additional benefits like dental, hearing, or vision coverage in your Medicare plan?\n10. How often do you typically need to see a specialist or require hospital care? This will help us gauge the level of coverage you might require.'),(9,'ali','haider','2025-01-31','','',NULL,'street 12 ','USA','california','61166','565655656456','ali@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'fatima',2,0,1,0,0,'2025-02-28 10:54:28','2025-02-28 10:57:38','Haris Ellahi','completed','1. Mr. Ali, could you share your current financial goals and how your existing life insurance plan aligns with them?\n2. Could you share your concerns or any apprehensions you might have about your current life insurance plan?\n3. Are you aware of any changes to your life circumstances that might necessitate a change in your life insurance policy?\n4. What are the key factors, in your opinion, that you consider important when choosing a life insurance plan?\n5. Are there any specific aspects of your current life insurance policy that you\'re dissatisfied with?\n6. How comfortable are you with your current understanding of your life insurance policy\'s terms and benefits?\n7. Mr. Ali, given that your campaign interest is life insurance, do you have any plans to expand or diversify your insurance portfolio?\n8. Do you foresee any significant life changes in the near future, such as marriage, having a child, or retirement, which might require an adjustment of your life insurance coverage?\n9. Are there any family members or dependents whose financial needs you’re particularly concerned about in the event of your demise?\n10. Lastly, how can I best assist you in achieving your financial goals with respect to your life insurance planning?'),(10,'faraz','khan','2025-01-29','','',NULL,'gdshdghs','asgdhsg','ghsdgh','65','523642534253','faraz@gmail.com',NULL,NULL,'saad',2,0,0,0,1,'2025-02-28 11:49:12','2025-02-28 11:52:44','Haris Ellahi','completed','1. What are your primary goals when it comes to long-term care planning? Are you more focused on maintaining your independence, ensuring comfort, securing financial stability, or something else?\n2. Have you already taken any steps towards planning for your long-term care? If so, could you please mention what these steps are?\n3. What are your biggest concerns or fears when you think about your long-term care needs?\n4. Do you have any health conditions we should take into account while planning for your long-term care?\n5. Are there any specific living arrangements you would prefer for your long-term care, such as aging in place, assisted living, or a nursing home?\n6. Have you discussed your long-term care plans with your family? If so, could you share any insights or decisions that have been made from these discussions?\n7. What is your current understanding of Medicare\'s coverage for long-term care expenses?\n8. Have you considered how you will finance your long-term care? Are there any specific resources or assets you plan to use?\n9. Do you have any particular preferences or concerns about the type of long-term care services you might need, such as home care, adult day care, or hospice care?\n10. How important is it for you to include wealth preservation strategies in your long-term care planning? Would you like to explore options to protect your assets while ensuring you receive the care you need?');
